#: ../../upstream/docs/user/security-implications.rst:2
msgid "Security considerations for documentation pages"
msgstr "文档页面的安全考量"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/security-implications.rst:4
msgid ""
"This article explains the security implications of documentation pages, this"
" doesn't apply to the main dashboard (readthedocs.org/readthedocs.com), only"
" to documentation pages (readthedocs.io, readthedocs-hosted.com, and custom "
"domains)."
msgstr ""
"本文讲解文档页面的安全影响。这不适用于主仪表盘（readthedocs.org/readthedocs.com），仅适用于文档页面（readthedocs.io"
"、readthedocs-hosted.com 及自定义域名）。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/security-implications.rst:10
msgid ":doc:`/api/cross-site-requests`"
msgstr ":doc:`/api/cross-site-requests`"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/security-implications.rst:11
msgid "Learn about cross-origin requests in our public APIs."
msgstr "了解我们公共 API 中的跨源请求。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/security-implications.rst:14
msgid "Cross-origin requests"
msgstr "跨源请求"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/security-implications.rst:16
msgid ""
"Read the Docs allows `cross-origin requests`_ for documentation resources it"
" serves. However, internal and proxied APIs, typically found under the "
"``/_/`` path don't allow cross-origin requests."
msgstr ""
"Read the Docs 允许对其提供的文档资源发起 `cross-origin requests`_ 。但内部和代理 API（通常在 ``/_/``"
" 路径下）不允许跨源请求。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/security-implications.rst:19
msgid ""
"To facilitate this, the following headers are added to all responses from "
"documentation pages:"
msgstr "为实现这一点，文档页面的所有响应都会添加以下标头："

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/security-implications.rst:21
msgid "``Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *``"
msgstr "``Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *``"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/security-implications.rst:22
msgid "``Access-Control-Allow-Methods: GET, HEAD, OPTIONS``"
msgstr "``Access-Control-Allow-Methods: GET, HEAD, OPTIONS``"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/security-implications.rst:24
msgid ""
"These headers allow cross-origin requests from any origin and only allow the"
" GET, HEAD and OPTIONS methods. It's important to note that passing "
"credentials (such as cookies or HTTP authentication) in cross-origin "
"requests is not allowed, ensuring access to public resources only."
msgstr ""
"这些标头允许来自任意源的跨源请求，但仅允许 GET、HEAD 和 OPTIONS 方法。需注意跨源请求中不允许传递凭据（如 cookie 或 HTTP "
"认证），确保只能访问公开资源。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/security-implications.rst:30
msgid ""
"Having cross-origin requests enabled allows third-party websites to make use"
" of files from your documentation (as long as they are public), which allows"
" various third-party integrations to work."
msgstr "启用跨源请求后，第三方网站可使用你文档中的文件（只要是公开的），从而让各种第三方集成得以工作。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/security-implications.rst:33
msgid ""
"If needed, the ``Access-Control`` headers can be changed for your "
"documentation pages by :doc:`contacting support </support>`. **You are "
"responsible for providing the correct values for these headers, and making "
"sure they don't break your documentation pages.**"
msgstr ""
"如需要，可通过 :doc:`联系支持 </support>` 更改文档页面的 ``Access-Control`` "
"标头。**你需负责提供这些标头的正确值，并确保它们不会破坏你的文档页面。**"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/security-implications.rst:39
msgid "Cookies"
msgstr "Cookie"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/security-implications.rst:41
msgid "On |org_brand|, we don't use cookies, as all resources are public."
msgstr "|org_brand| 不使用 cookie，因为所有资源都是公开的。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/security-implications.rst:43
msgid ""
"On |com_brand|, we use cookies to store user sessions. These cookies are set"
" when a user authenticates to access private documentation. Session cookies "
"have the ``SameSite`` attribute set to ``None``, which allows them to be "
"sent in cross-origin requests where allowed (see :ref:`security-implications"
":Cross-origin requests`), for example, when embedding private documentation "
"pages in an iframe (see :ref:`security-implications:Embedding documentation "
"pages`)."
msgstr ""
"|com_brand| 使用 cookie 存储用户会话。这些 cookie 在用户认证以访问私有文档时设置。会话 cookie 的 "
"``SameSite`` 属性设为 ``None`` ，允许在允许的情况下随跨源请求发送（见 :ref:`security-implications"
":Cross-origin requests` ），例如将私有文档页面嵌入 iframe 时（见 :ref:`security-"
"implications:Embedding documentation pages` ）。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/security-implications.rst:52
msgid "Embedding documentation pages"
msgstr "嵌入文档页面"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/security-implications.rst:54
msgid ""
"Embedding documentation pages in an iframe is allowed. Read the Docs doesn't"
" set the ``X-Frame-Options`` or ``Content-Security-Policy`` headers, which "
"means that the browser's default behavior is used."
msgstr ""
"允许将文档页面嵌入 iframe。Read the Docs 不设置 ``X-Frame-Options`` 或 ``Content-Security-"
"Policy`` 标头，因此采用浏览器的默认行为。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/security-implications.rst:58
msgid ""
"Embedding private documentation pages in an iframe is possible, but it "
"requires users to be previously authenticated in the embedded domain."
msgstr "可以将私有文档页面嵌入 iframe，但要求用户此前已在被嵌入域中完成认证。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/security-implications.rst:61
msgid ""
"It's important to note that embedding documentation pages in an iframe does "
"not grant the parent page access the iframe's content. Documentation pages "
"serve static content only, and the exposed APIs are read-only, making the "
"exploitation of a clickjacking vulnerability extremely unlikely."
msgstr ""
"需注意，将文档页面嵌入 iframe 并不会赋予父页面访问 iframe 内容的能力。文档页面只提供静态内容，暴露的 API "
"为只读，因此点击劫持漏洞被利用的可能性极低。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/security-implications.rst:65
msgid ""
"If needed, the ``X-Frame-Options`` and ``Content-Security-Policy`` headers "
"can be set on your documentation pages by :doc:`contacting support "
"</support>`. **You are responsible for providing the correct values for "
"these headers, and making sure they don't break your documentation pages.**"
msgstr ""
"如需要，可通过 :doc:`联系支持 </support>` 在文档页面上设置 ``X-Frame-Options`` 和 ``Content-"
"Security-Policy`` 标头。**你需负责提供这些标头的正确值，并确保它们不会破坏你的文档页面。**"

